#
# ==============================================================================
# STEP 03 -- ANALYSIS 3: TWO-WAY FIXED EFFECTS MODELS (M1-M23)
# Annual multi-crop panel: TMX_ann, PRE_ann, no phenology, no VPD
#
# 8 crops x 23 models = 184 estimates (production-weighted, unless noted)
#
# CENTERING: TMX_ann and PRE_ann are mean-centered (per crop, using that
# crop's own estimation sample mean) BEFORE squaring, following the
# centering convention in Schlenker & Roberts (2009, PNAS) ("curves are
# centered so that the exposure-weighted impact is zero"). This does not
# change the shape of the estimated response curve, fitted values, or the
# quadratic coefficient itself -- it only removes the structural collinearity
# between a variable and its own square (confirmed in Step02: TMX/TMX2 raw
# r > 0.98, VIF up to 77), and makes the linear coefficient interpretable
# as the marginal effect AT THE SAMPLE MEAN rather than at TMX=0 degC (a
# point with no physical meaning in this context).
#
#   TMX_c  = TMX_ann - mean(TMX_ann)   | TMX_sq = TMX_c^2
#   PRE_c  = PRE_ann - mean(PRE_ann)   | PRE_sq = PRE_c^2
#
# MODEL TABLE (full equations):
#
#  Block A -- linear TMX, linear PRE
#   M1  ln_yield = a + b1*TMX_c + b2*PRE_c + FE(country) + FE(year)
#   M2  M1 + b3*IRR
#   M3  M1 + b3*ln_gdp                              [GDP subsample]
#   M4  M1 + b3*IRR + b4*ln_gdp   -- MAIN MODEL      [GDP subsample]
#
#  Block B -- TMX + TMX^2 (centered), linear PRE
#   M5  ln_yield = a + b1*TMX_c + b2*TMX_sq + b3*PRE_c + FE(country) + FE(year)
#   M6  M5 + b4*IRR
#   M7  M5 + b4*ln_gdp                               [GDP subsample]
#   M8  M5 + b4*IRR + b5*ln_gdp                       [GDP subsample]
#
#  Block C -- linear TMX, PRE + PRE^2 (centered)
#   M9  ln_yield = a + b1*TMX_c + b2*PRE_c + b3*PRE_sq + FE(country) + FE(year)
#   M10 M9 + b4*IRR
#   M11 M9 + b4*ln_gdp                                [GDP subsample]
#   M12 M9 + b4*IRR + b5*ln_gdp                        [GDP subsample]
#
#  Block D -- TMX + TMX^2, PRE + PRE^2 (both centered)
#   M13 ln_yield = a + b1*TMX_c + b2*TMX_sq + b3*PRE_c + b4*PRE_sq + FE(country) + FE(year)
#   M14 M13 + b5*IRR
#   M15 M13 + b5*ln_gdp                                [GDP subsample]
#   M16 M13 + b5*IRR + b6*ln_gdp                        [GDP subsample]
#
#  Block E -- robustness (all built on M4's variable set)          [GDP subsample]
#   M17 M4 + country-specific linear trend: + Country_ISO:Yil
#   M18 M4, outcome = detrended ln_yield (two-stage: residual after
#       removing country FE + country-specific linear year trend)
#   M19 M4, weights = baseline_production_tonnes (fixed 1990-2000-or-
#       fallback average, from Step00 -- avoids contemporaneous-weight
#       endogeneity concern)
#   M20 M4, weights = baseline_area_harvested_ha (same fixed baseline
#       window, area instead of production -- non-contemporaneous
#       area-weighted alternative)
#   M21 M4 + b5*(IRR x TMX_c)      -- does irrigation buffer heat damage?
#   M22 M4 + b5*(ln_gdp x TMX_c)   -- income-related adaptation signal?
#   M23 M4 + b5*(is_arid_fixed x TMX_c) -- structural aridity x heat?
#
# All interaction/robustness interpretations are SUGGESTIVE, not causal
# adaptation evidence (cf. reviewer checklist item on policy/adaptation
# claims staying suggestive).
#
# Plots: G_M1 (TMX_c forest, M1-M4, all crops), G_M2 (coefficient
# significance heatmap, all models x all crops)
#   -- Saved: PDF + PNG 1600dpi x labeled + unlabeled, into the single
#      shared figures_paperv2/ folder used by every step
#
# References:
#   Schlenker & Roberts (2009, PNAS) -- centering convention, nonlinear TMX
#   Lobell et al. (2011, Science)    -- benchmark TMX coefficient
#   Dell et al. (2014, AER)          -- two-way FE identification
#   Burke & Emerick (2016, AEJ)      -- panel design
# ==============================================================================


