# ==============================================================================
# STEP 04 -- ANALYSIS 4: TMX / PRE RESPONSE CURVES + OPTIMAL POINT
# Annual multi-crop panel: TMX_ann, PRE_ann, no phenology, no VPD
#
# BUG FIX (this version): the sample filter below was missing the
# `area_harvested_ha > 0` condition that Step03 applies when estimating
# M13 (and every other model). This meant Step04 was independently
# re-estimating M13 on a DIFFERENT (larger, less-filtered) sample than
# Step03's own M13 -- the same class of error discovered and fixed in
# Step05. The filter now matches Step03's exactly. A cross-check against
# Step03's saved M13 TMX_c coefficient has also been added (see the end
# of the main loop) so any future drift between the two scripts is
# caught immediately, in console output, rather than silently.
#
# Uses the M13 specification (TMX_c + TMX_sq + PRE_c + PRE_sq | Country_ISO
# + Yil, full sample, production-weighted) as the basis for the response
# curves. This is re-estimated here (rather than read from Step03)
# because building the response-curve confidence bands requires the full
# coefficient covariance matrix (specifically Cov(TMX_c, TMX_sq)), which
# Step03's saved Excel output does not include -- only point estimates
# and standard errors.
#
# Response curve: predicted change in ln(yield), relative to the sample
# mean, holding the other variable at ITS sample mean. Curves are
# centered so the effect is exactly 0 at each variable's own sample mean
# (Schlenker & Roberts 2009 convention).
#
# Confidence bands: delta method on the quadratic form,
#   Var(effect) = x^2*Var(b1) + x^4*Var(b2) + 2*x^3*Cov(b1,b2)
# using the model's country-clustered variance-covariance matrix.
#
# Optimal point: x* = -b1 / (2*b2). Reliable only when (a) quadratic
# coefficient p<0.10, (b) turning point within observed data range, and
# (c) negative quadratic coefficient (inverted-U). Otherwise explicitly
# labeled unreliable / implausible sign rather than presented as a
# well-identified optimum.
#
# Plots: G_R1, G_R2, G_R3 -- saved PDF + PNG 1600dpi, labeled + unlabeled.
# ==============================================================================


